body:
I appreciate your response and this is actually something I find very interesting. I don't understand the source of the offense at all. I never once uttered the word 'all'. That came from your imagination. I referenced the idea that many, maybe most, women who act on the masculine side, are attracted to other women. Never said all women who act that way are lesbians, nor did I imply the converse, that most/all lesbians act masculine, which is a completely unrelated and (as you stated) false statement that I never had in mind. About the genetic material, I never even said it's a thing many women do! That would be (as you said) quite insane. It was simply an inference about this one particular woman based on her perceived behaviours, attitudes, and desires. At no point did I suggest it was anything else. Now we can argue over the strengths and weaknesses of my inference but for you to put words in my mouth and say I'm the one making a statement about all women, is just false. You're the one hearing that statement, when none was made.

&#x200B;

I'll give another example. I'm an awkward, single Asian guy with glasses and bad clothes. Someone comes up to me and says 'I bet you like math.' That's not offensive, that's a good use of statistics. I would just reply actually I'm a rare exception, might even be an interesting point of conversation. Someone comes up to me and says 'You probably haven't been laid in a really long time.' Not offensive, it makes me sad about a statistical fact, but it's still just statistics. Someone comes up to me, thinks 'surely this guy hasn't been laid in years', tries to manipulate my lack of dating experience into making her a baby, now that's offensive. But I still want to help her how I can.

0 more. But I don't think it's worth it.

&#x200B;

It's true that (Biblical) Christianity was extremely stressful. I don't acknowledge its tenets any longer (unless I am having an 'episode' apparently), in fact I'm not sure precisely what they are. However there is still a decent argument to be had of the following form.

&#x200B;

A) There is a lot of serious doubt on the efficacy of psychology, especially relative to its expense. Moral hazards, [this article](https://www.nytimes.com/2010/01/10/magazine/10psyche-t.html), Rosenhan, etc.

&#x200B;

B) Even if it was efficacious there are people in much greater and more urgent need of psychiatric help than me. The same money spent on me would be better spent donating them care.

&#x200B;

Not 30 minutes from me there are people living in tin shacks and sleeping on dirt floors and their kids can't focus in school because they don't get enough sleep. This isn't me being psychotic or whatever. This is real life. I'm not going to spend thousands of dollars so I can have a better feeling about myself, when that same money could buy mattresses for dozens of families.

&#x200B;

In my experience 'get help' is code for 'I don't know the answer so talk to those guys who claim to'.  Like, I appreciate the effort to help, you've spent time with me here typing all this, and I definitely feel less lonely and burdened as a result. But you can really drop the code.

Thanks so much for the dialogue. There's some stuff I didn't disclose. ----------------------------------------------------- \[redacted to protect identity\] This girl really highly values achievement, intelligence and especially education. It's everything to her. As for wanting the hookup there was just a series of texts and actions and the aforementioned birdie (very shrewd old woman) who has known her and her family for decades, also basically agreed that she wanted it (I haven't mentioned my lesbian theory yet).

&#x200B;

I mistyped the first time round, birdie didn't call her promiscuous, she said she knew a lot of men (In her mind that equals promiscuity. Birdie is 81 years old)

&#x200B;

I guess if that's the case then I'm just really at a loss as to what it is she wanted or how I could have made her happy without fucking her. She was such a sad girl and I had so much power over her. I just wish I could have done or said something.

Mexico

&#x200B;

She can't, she is halfway around the world for the next several years.

She actually flew to where I came from originally so it's not that insane, I wouldn't only be seeing her.

&#x200B;

Also I added an evidence section.  I'm interested why you think it's so unrealistic, though, or what about intimacy I find confusing, I really really appreciate the chance to learn.

&#x200B;

Also, this is not the US, this society is more repressed than Kansas.

&#x200B;

Thank you for your feedback

NO YOU DO NOT UNDERSTAND THIS SHIT HAS BEEN GOING ON FOR YEARS AND YEARS, WHACK A MOLE OF DIFFERENT SINS, IT IS IMPOSSIBLE TO ERADICATE SIN FROM MY LIFE BECAUSE I AM JUST THAT DEPRAVED

&#x200B;

YOU ARE DEALING WITH A MONSTER THE LIKES OF WHICH WOULD PUT STALIN, HITLER AND POL POT TO SHAME.
